What FAISS actually does

It is a library for:

Efficient nearest neighbor search in high-dimensional vector space

Translation:

Given a vector → find the most similar vectors.

Where it’s used

Chatbots (memory / RAG)

Semantic search

Recommendation systems

Face recognition

Document search

Duplicate detection

Basically: anything using embeddings.

One-line definition

FAISS is a library for fast similarity search over large collections of vectors (embeddings).
